// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - JenniferNobleClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P532444358" "Jennifer Noble"
// DetailString :
"P2141832424" "According to the Noble Savage, he is married to a woman named Jennifer Noble. He told you that as proof you should recite the inscription on the inside of her wedding band.<br><br><color lightseagreen>You are my guiding light - James</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WarehouseMeetClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1079542675" "Barnum & Co. warehouse"
// DetailString :
"P143011349" "Jennifer agreed to meet the man claiming to be her deceased husband in a neutral location, the Barnum & Co. warehouse."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - HappySavageClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2688208607" "Happy Savage"
// DetailString :
"P3335545195" "After telling James Noble that his wife, Jennifer, would meet with him, he seemed truly happy. Perhaps he really is who he claims to be."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1706753127" "The Noble Savage"
// DetailString :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ItsATrapClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2577927888" "It's a Trap!"
// DetailString :
"P1359647498" "Too late you realized that the empty warehouse that Jennifer Noble agreed to meet at was a PPD trap designed to take the Noble Savage down."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SavageFleesClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P513556993" "Gone in a Rage"
// DetailString :
"P927231603" "After fighting off a PPD ambush the Noble Savage flew into a rage and raced off to who knows where. He probably thinks you set this whole thing up. You'd better figure out what's really going on before you go after him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PerkinsClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1105831880" "Sergeant Perkins "
// DetailString :
"P3391466753" "Sergeant Perkins had this to say.<br><br><color lightseagreen>I still can't believe he's alive. James Noble was the best officer I had ever known. He was strong, passionate, and he lived up to his name. He was truly noble.<br><br>When he died, or at least, we were told that he died, Jenny, his wife, went to pieces. I wanted to console her, but the only person she really opened up to was Jim Donner, James' partner and best friend.<br><br>They, um, they grew close. Got married a few months back.<br><br>Jim is a captain now... wait!<br><br>This operation was put into motion by Jim Donner! Oh man, Donner must have been in on Noble's death from the beginning! He claimed to be witness to Noble's death.<br><br>When Noble finds out what Donner has done...<br><br>I know where he's heading, to go see his wife. You've got to stop him before someone gets killed! I'll keep the PPD off your back.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - JimDonnerClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P479127413" "Captain Jim Donner"
// DetailString :
"P1123803365" "According to Sergeant Perkins, Captain Jim Donner approved the mission to take out James Noble, the Noble Savage. He also happened to be James Noble's best friend and partner, claimed he was a witness to Noble's death at the hands of Resistance terrorists, and then married Noble's wife, Jennifer.<br><br>This scumbag is going to get what he deserves."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - JenniferDonnerClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P71848456" "Jennifer Donner"
// DetailString :
"P1347492241" "Jennifer Noble became Jennifer Donner when she married Jim Donner, her deceased husband's best friend and partner. You can only imagine the mixture of guilt, rage, anguish, and confusion that this poor woman is feeling right now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - NickClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P855244289" "Nick Noble"
// DetailString :
"P633911326" "James Noble's son, Nick Noble, was never convinced that his father died the way they said he did. His mother's marriage to his dad's best friend and partner only enraged him more, turning his already bumpy teenage angst into a serious problem with authority. When Nick found out his father was still alive, he changed. His doubt and anger turned to courage and love. You have a feeling that Praetoria City has more to hear from Nick Noble in the near future."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - NobleSavageClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3272755780" "James Noble, The Noble Savage"
// DetailString :
"P3803795706" "James Noble was once the pride of the PPD, the poster child of the law, a flawless example whom all who wore the badge were measured against. When Neuron asked James to volunteer for top secret experimental procedure to improve the efficiency of the PPD, James jumped at the chance to do his duty and help others in bettering Praetoria.<br><br>But the procedure went horribly wrong. James was pronounced dead on Neuron's operating table, and his body was dumped into the tunnels. Since nobody knew James was undergoing the proceedure, it was easy enough to spin the death of Praetoria's most loved policeman as a horrible act by the Resistance terrorists rumored to be forming beneath Praetoria's streets.<br><br>But James Noble didn't die that day. Neuron's proceedure did work, partially. James' body started to mutate, and in the process, his body sprang back to life. Dissoriented and confused, James wandered the tunnels unsure of who or what he was.<br><br>It would take months for the memories to resurface in James' mind. Until then, however, his attempts to explore the city streets were too often met with horrified citizens and then the sound of PPD boots coming his way. He stole what he could to survive, made alliances with the denizens of the tunnels where they could be made, and eventually took to fighting wrongs wherever he found them, his noble nature shining through despite his horrific exterior.<br><br>When his memories had fully returned, James knew that the wrong done against him and his family needed to be righted. His first step was to make sure his wife and son knew he was alive. Little did James know that such a small act would cause an avalanche of trouble to come crashing down around him."

